{{- /*
ships-in-container.tmpl — the ONE answer to "does this entry belong in a worker image?"

Input (dict):
  ctx   required; root chezmoi context
  tool  required; a commands.units `tool:` value, or a unit id for a unit that
        declares no tool. Companion artifacts of a primary tool (bunx from bun,
        uvx from uv, sg from ast-grep, the buf man page and completions) pass
        their PRIMARY tool's name -- they ship exactly when it does, and an alias
        table would be a second place to forget.

Emits the literal "true" or "false".

WHY THIS EXISTS. .chezmoidata/commands.yaml already carried `gate: "!container"`,
but only command-manifest.tmpl read it, and a command link is not a payload: the
external still downloaded into the image and the gate withheld nothing but a
symlink. The externals files now ask the same question through this partial, so
one declaration governs both the download and the link. Gate ASSIGNMENT stays
data in commands.yaml; gate RESOLUTION is here, exactly as facts.yaml splits them.

AN UNKNOWN TOOL FAILS THE RENDER. The alternative is that a typo answers "ship
it", which is silent and lands in a published image.
*/ -}}
{{- if not (kindIs "map" .) -}}
{{-   fail (printf "ships-in-container.tmpl: expected a dict, got %s" (kindOf .)) -}}
{{- end -}}
{{- range $required := list "ctx" "tool" -}}
{{-   if not (hasKey $ (printf "%s" $required)) -}}
{{-     fail (printf "ships-in-container.tmpl: %s is required" $required) -}}
{{-   end -}}
{{- end -}}
{{- $ctx := .ctx -}}
{{- $tool := .tool -}}
{{- $facts := includeTemplate "facts.tmpl" $ctx | fromYaml -}}
{{- $found := false -}}
{{- $ships := true -}}
{{- range $unitId, $unit := $ctx.commands.units -}}
{{-   $names := list $unitId -}}
{{-   if hasKey $unit "tool" -}}{{- $names = append $names $unit.tool -}}{{- end -}}
{{-   if has $tool $names -}}
{{-     $found = true -}}
{{-     if hasKey $unit "gate" -}}
{{-       if and (eq $unit.gate "!container") $facts.container -}}
{{-         $ships = false -}}
{{-       end -}}
{{-     end -}}
{{-   end -}}
{{- end -}}
{{- if not $found -}}
{{-   fail (printf "ships-in-container.tmpl: %q names no unit id and no unit tool in .chezmoidata/commands.yaml; declare the unit or pass its primary tool" $tool) -}}
{{- end -}}
{{- $ships -}}
